  "description": "Guides to the customs behind buying gold and silver for Pidyon HaBen, Dhanteras, Lunar New Year, Las Arras, gold sovereigns and anniversary gifts.",
  "canonical": "https://bulliontradingllc.com/traditions/",
  "text": "Bullion Trading Traditions\nTraditions\nThe cultural, religious, and life-event reasons families come to us for silver and gold — explained plainly, with the halacha and the metal in one place.\nAnniversary Gifts by Year — Silver, Gold & the Metal Milestones\nThe year-by-year wedding-anniversary gift list — the metal milestones (Silver 25th, Gold 50th, Platinum 70th), gemstone years, and a keepsake that lasts.\nRead the guide →\nLas Arras & Mexican Gold — the 13 Wedding Coins\nThe 13 wedding coins (las arras) explained — their origin, the meaning of thirteen, the padrinos, and Mexico’s gold: the Centenario and Hidalgo pesos.\nRead the guide →\nThe 21st-Birthday Gold Sovereign — Britain’s “Key of the Door”\nWhy the gold sovereign is Britain’s classic 21st-birthday “key of the door” gift — Pistrucci’s St George, the guinea link, and the modern revivals.\nRead the guide →\nLunar New Year Gold — Year of the Horse 2026\nA guide to gold and silver for Lunar New Year — the zodiac and rare Fire Horse, red-envelope etiquette, lucky numbers, and what to give by recipient.\nRead the guide →\nDhanteras — The Most Auspicious Day to Buy Gold & Silver\nA plain-English guide to buying gold and silver for Dhanteras and Diwali — the legends, the five days, what to buy by budget, plus weights and timing.\nRead the guide →\nPidyon HaBen — The Redemption of the Firstborn Son\nA plain-English guide to Pidyon HaBen — the mitzvah, the five silver shekels, the 31st day, and the ceremony — for families redeeming a firstborn son.\nRead the guide →",
